# Agent workflow (mandatory)

Agents and cloud workers **must** follow this workflow. Completing a task by violating architecture rules is **forbidden** — CI and `pnpm audit:module-architecture` are the gate, not README checkboxes or issue “done” lists.

## 1. Never work outside the rules

**Forbidden shortcuts** (non-exhaustive):

- Copying **`apps/studio/src/module/*`**, **`packages/orpc/src/modules/*`**, or legacy app **`lib/*`** as templates for **new** product code
- New **tRPC** procedures, **`z.unknown()`** oRPC inputs, controllers without **`serviceResponseSchema(...).parse`**, domain logic in **`apps/*/src/app/**/page.tsx`**
- “Temporary” adapters that skip **`runAction`**, audit, or ServiceResponse to ship faster
- Marking an issue complete while leaving **new** architecture audit violations

**Required:** [AGENTS.md](../AGENTS.md), [docs/gaps/forbidden-defaults.md](../docs/gaps/forbidden-defaults.md), [docs/new-feature-checklist.md](../docs/new-feature-checklist.md), and **`pnpm audit:module-architecture`** (exit 0).

## 2. Parent issue → sub-issues (chunks)

- One **parent** GitHub issue describes the outcome; **implementation work is split into sub-issues** (one verifiable slice each).
- Agents implement **one sub-issue per session** when possible; do not boil the ocean in a single PR.
- Sub-issue body must name **`module/<domain>/`** and link the parent issue.

## 3. Branch, commits, merge gate

| Step | Rule |
|------|------|
| Branch | From **`dev`**: `feat/<parent>-<short-slug>` or `fix/<parent>-<short-slug>` (include parent issue number) |
| Commits | **One commit per completed sub-issue**; footer **`Fixes #<sub-issue>`** (use **`Refs #<parent>`** when the parent stays open) |
| PR | Targets **`dev`** only; lists sub-issues closed by the PR |
| Before merge | Run **`pnpm verify:dev-merge`** on the **full branch diff** (all sub-issues on that branch), not only the last commit |

Do not merge to **`dev`** until verification passes on the combined branch work for that parent issue.

## 4. Plan before code (especially small / fast models)

Before editing files:

1. Read **`module/<domain>/README.md`** for that domain (workflow, boundaries, TODOs).
2. Read the **sub-issue** acceptance criteria only — not the whole parent scope.
3. If scope is large for the model (e.g. Tera, Luna, or any “light” agent): write a **short plan** in the chat (ordered steps mapping to checklist sections 1–8 in [new-feature-checklist.md](../docs/new-feature-checklist.md)) and execute **one step at a time**.
4. Switch to **Plan mode** when the sub-issue touches more than ~3 layers (utils + server + oRPC + client + routes).

## 5. Migration: new structure only

We are moving from legacy app/API folders to **`module/<domain>/`**. For **new or migrated** code:

- **Do not** extend legacy patterns “because it still exists”
- **Do not** add product logic under **`packages/orpc/src/modules/<domain>`** or fat Studio app modules
- Compatibility shims (tRPC/MCP unwrap) are **transport-only** — new behavior lives in **`module/`** + thin oRPC

## 6. Reference code: module first

When looking for examples:

1. **`module/<same-or-close-domain>/`** (e.g. teams pilot)
2. **`module/shared/`**
3. **`docs/gaps/*`** and platform **`packages/`** (infra only)

**Last resort:** legacy paths — read-only to understand behavior, **never** as a copy template.

## 7. Blocked dependencies → module README TODO

If work depends on another domain not yet migrated or an open issue:

- **Stop** at the boundary; do not fake completion with app-layer hacks
- Add a **`## TODO (blocked)`** entry in **`module/<domain>/README.md`**: dependency, sub-issue or issue link, what remains
- In code, prefer a **single** `// TODO(#issue): …` pointing to that README section — no silent partial implementations

## 8. Module README is the operational source of truth

Per-domain **plans, migration boundaries, verification commands, and TODOs** live in **`module/<domain>/README.md`**, not new long-form docs under **`docs/`**.

- **`docs/`** = platform-wide contracts, gaps index, naming — **not** duplicate module runbooks
- When changing how a module is built or verified, **update that module’s README** in the same PR

Template: [module/README.template.md](../module/README.template.md).

